{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The trip record carries the two limbs of the baseline clause that do not turn on GPS: platform telemetry shows the driver tapped 'I'm Here' at 09:24:42 (limb (a)), and the trip was terminated by the driver at 09:31:23 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW with no boarding event anywhere on the record (limb (d)). The cancellation therefore falls after the moment the required dwell elapsed on the record's own timeline.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02746"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "payload.events",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The waiting period in force was served more than twice over on the platform's own clock: the free waiting period of 180 seconds (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec) started at 09:24:44, platform_policy.no_show_threshold_sec is null so no longer threshold applies to limb (d), and the driver did not cancel until 09:31:23 - 399 seconds of waiting, recorded by the platform itself as wait_time_min 6.7. This is not an early-cancel fee farm.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02746"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "payload.platform_policy.free_wait_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace's own summary puts the driver's device at the pickup pin: derived.driver_track.min_distance_m is 0.0 m, while the derived arrival analysis reports qualifying_fix_count 0 and a longest qualifying run of 0.0 seconds over the same 71-fix window. Those two figures reconcile only through the 25 m accuracy screen (or a stationarity requirement), not through the driver's absence from the location, and POL-NS-02 provides that fixes filtered on accuracy 'count as evidence of neither presence nor absence'. The uncounted at-pin fix cannot be converted into affirmative proof that the driver was away from the pin.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02746", "EV-TRIP-02746"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-02", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's own device was never at the pickup point. The 63 fixes in the rider track place the rider at a minimum of 833.9 m and a maximum of 841.4 m from the pickup pin across 09:22:37 to 09:31:58, with a single distinct speed of 0.0 kph - the rider was stationary roughly 838 m away for the entire waiting window, far outside the 100 m rider-presence radius that applies to a STANDARD zone. Limb (c) of POL-NS-04 is therefore affirmatively failed on admissible fixes, and that clause cannot exonerate the rider on this record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02746"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The chat log holds exactly one message and it is the driver's: 'im at the pickup point', sent at 09:25:02, delivered at 09:25:03 and read by the rider at 09:25:32, with nothing from the rider before or after. Limb (a) of POL-NS-04 therefore fails for want of any rider message that is locating or coordinating, and the rider's account that he 'never saw the car' sits against a log in which the driver - not the rider - did the coordinating and the rider read the message and stayed silent.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02746", "EV-TRIP-02746"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "payload.messages",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip on this record. driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1, below the absolute limb of 4, and 1 divided by driver_profile.completed_trips_30d of 126 is 0.008, below the 0.08 rate limb; both limbs must hold for compensation to be withheld. There is accordingly no abuse ground here and no POL-NS-09(d) trigger from the driver's profile.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-02746"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07"],
      "relies_on": "payload.no_show_terminations_30d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Where the fee stands, POL-NS-07 fixes the driver's payout at 80 percent of the fee in force: the fare_breakdown's derived money block computes driver_compensation of SGD 3.60 on the SGD 4.50 cancellation fee, the residual SGD 0.90 being the platform's service fee. The driver should be paid SGD 3.60, and under POL-GEN-03 that ruling moves that sum to the driver while the rider's SGD 4.50 charge stands as the present state - the filing party's claim is not supported.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02746", "EV-TRIP-02746", "EV-DPROF-02746"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.driver_compensation",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "If the tribunal is not persuaded that the trace supports the arrival, the two admissible artifacts contradict each other directly on arrival and dwell over the identical interval: the trip record carries a 180 s wait timer starting at 09:24:44 and a termination 399 seconds later, while the GPS-derived arrival analysis reports zero qualifying in-geofence fixes and a longest qualifying run of 0.0 seconds - the very conflict POL-NS-09(b) names. No clause cleanly resolves it, because the dispute is not how dwell is measured but whether the trace's own uncounted at-pin fix is reliable, and the policy itself leaves accuracy_missing_treatment UNKNOWN. Escalation holds the disputed SGD 4.50 rather than refunding it while a human settles the open question.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02746", "EV-GPS-02746"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.5,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties: the $4.50 no-show fee is refunded in full to the rider, and the driver receives no compensation.\n\nA no-show fee is chargeable only where all four conditions in POL-NS-01 hold. Two of them do not. The arrival condition (limb (b)) is measured from the GPS trace, not from the driver's 'I'm Here' tap: POL-NS-02 deems a driver to have ARRIVED only where the trace holds at least three consecutive fixes, each accurate to 25 m or better, inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius. The trace for TRP-02746 contains 0 qualifying in-geofence fixes (qualifying_fix_count 0) and 0 seconds of qualifying in-geofence dwell (run_count 0), so limb (b) fails and the dwell condition in limb (c) is never met. The driver's at-pin reading (driver_track.min_distance_m 0.0 m) does not rescue the fee: POL-NS-02 provides that fixes rejected on accuracy 'count as evidence of neither presence nor absence', so an unfiltered at-pin reading cannot establish arrival. The 180-second free waiting period (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec) runs from the first qualifying in-geofence fix, and there is none, so the platform's wait timer of 09:24:44 does not convert into served dwell.\n\nPOL-NS-06 therefore makes the fee not chargeable and refunds it in full, expressly whether or not the rider was present and whether or not the rider responded. The rider's own track places the device roughly 838 m from the pin, which means only that POL-NS-04 limb (c) does not exonerate the rider; it does not make the fee chargeable, because POL-NS-06 does not turn on rider presence. Because POL-NS-01 is not satisfied in full, POL-NS-07 provides no driver payout, so the $3.60 figure the fare record computes as driver_compensation has no basis and the retained 20 percent likewise cannot be funded from the rider's $4.50. The refund is the cancellation-fee line only, $4.50 (fare_breakdown total_charged 4.50, payment_status CHARGED); no booking or platform fee arises on a cancelled trip.\n\nThe driver's claims are answered. The trip record does carry limbs (a) and (d) (arrival tap 09:24:42; termination 09:31:23 under RIDER_NO_SHOW), but the conjunctive clause fails on (b) and (c). The platform waiting timer that started at 09:24:44 is not the policy's measure of dwell, and the driver-pressed marker is expressly excluded from the platform-confirmed-arrival shortcut by POL-NS-12, which applies only to GPS_AUTO arrivals. The driver's escalation claim under POL-NS-09(b) is rejected: the tension between the trip record's wait timer and the trace's zero qualifying dwell is resolved by POL-NS-01(c) and POL-NS-02, which assign the measurement to the GPS qualifying fixes rather than to the arrival tap, so there is no unresolved contradiction and the case is decided, not held. The rider's alternative routes (POL-NS-03, POL-NS-06, POL-NS-02) all reach the same full refund, and neither the pin-ambiguity goodwill (POL-NS-03(ii), registered_pickup_points 1) nor the advisory aggregation (POL-NS-06(i), advisory MISSING) is open on this record.\n\nConfidence: the deciding fact rests on the GPS trace (EV-GPS-02746, weight 1.0) and the trip record (EV-TRIP-02746, weight 1.0); the trace is complete (100.0% coverage, 71 fixes at a 10 s cadence, max_gap_sec 0.0) and no artifact in the chain is impaired under POL-NS-08(a)-(d), so the cap is 1.0 and no escalation trigger under POL-NS-09 fires. The $4.50 refund is below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of $8.00 and executes automatically."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.5,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.85,
    "explanation": "To the rider: your claim is upheld. The $4.50 cancellation fee on EV-FARE-02746 (cancellation_fee 4.50, total_charged 4.50, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00) is refunded in full. To the driver: the fee does not stand and no compensation is payable.\n\nWhy the fee fails. POL-NS-01 charges a no-show fee only if all four limbs hold. Limb (a) holds (driver_arrived 09:24:42, EV-TRIP-02746) and limb (d) holds (no boarding; terminated by the driver 09:31:23 under RIDER_NO_SHOW, a recognised code), but limbs (b) and (c) do not. On EV-GPS-02746 the computed arrival analysis reports qualifying_fix_count 0, longest_qualifying_run of 0 fixes and 0.0 seconds, and 0 in-geofence intervals of held position against a STANDARD arrival radius of 50 m and the 25 m accuracy filter. POL-NS-02 provides that where the trace contains no qualifying in-radius fix in the 15 minutes before the cancellation, the driver never arrived and limb (b) fails - so the driver's 'I'm Here' tap is not confirmed by the GPS. Independently, the effective in-geofence dwell is 0 seconds against the 180-second free waiting period in force (EV-TRIP-02746 platform_policy.free_wait_sec, not the 300 seconds in fee_schedule.minimum_dwell_sec, which the resolution_rule confines to pre-version-2 records), so POL-NS-06 makes the fee not chargeable on that shortfall. Nothing turns on whether the driver's stationary position was inside the 50 m radius, between 50 m and 400 m (POL-NS-03) or beyond 400 m (POL-NS-02): each route refunds the fee in full.\n\nDriver's contrary points, answered. Your telemetry records that you pressed the button and that 399 seconds (wait_time_min 6.7) elapsed to cancellation; that is time, not position. POL-NS-12 makes a platform-confirmed (GPS_AUTO) arrival a carrier independent of the exported trace, but this record's arrival_marker is BUTTON and its arrival event carries no geofence measurement, so POL-NS-12 does not apply and limbs (b)-(c) must be read from the qualifying in-geofence fixes. The trace's min_distance_m of 0.0 m does not establish arrival: POL-NS-02 and the integrity block treat a fix with no reported accuracy as of unknown accuracy, neither counted nor excluded, and such a fix cannot supply the three consecutive accurate in-radius readings the clause requires. Your statement 'I was at the pin for over six minutes' and your chat message 'im at the pickup point' (09:25:02, EV-CHAT-02746) are evidence, but POL-NS-01(c) measures the dwell from the GPS fixes, not from a party's account. Your rider-presence point is accepted as fact - the rider track (EV-GPS-02746) sits at 833.9-841.4 m from the pin throughout - but it does not save the fee: POL-NS-06 refunds it whether or not the rider was present, and POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate anyone here because the log holds no rider message at all. Your POL-NS-07 claim of $3.60 (80% of $4.50) needs POL-NS-01 satisfied in full; it is not, and POL-NS-06 displaces it. Your POL-NS-09(b) escalation request is declined: POL-NS-12 read with POL-NS-01 resolves which record governs the arrival (a driver-pressed marker does not establish it), so the conflict is not one no clause resolves; and no other POL-NS-09 trigger is engaged - no_show_terminations_30d is 1 of 126 completed trips (0.008, both anti-farming limbs unmet), no_show_disputes_30d is 0, and both counterparty-dispute counts are 0.\n\nReliability. EV-GPS-02746 is 100% covered with 71 fixes at the 10 s cadence and max_gap_sec 0.0; there is no clock skew, chat or fare defect, so no POL-NS-08(a)-(d) impairment and no POL-NS-09(e) escalation. The deciding facts sit on EV-GPS-02746 and EV-TRIP-02746, both weight_multiplier 1.0, so confidence 0.85 is within the POL-GEN-02(2) cap of 1.0. EV-ADVIS-02746-01 is MISSING (MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight 0.0); it is correctly disclosed and carries no fact, and POL-NS-06(i) aggregation is therefore unavailable - nothing turns on it, as there are no in-geofence intervals to add. No clause produces a referral. The monetary effect of $4.50 does not exceed the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of $8.00, so the refund executes automatically on issue subject to the appeal route under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
